  user_input {
    user_response: "GOOGLE AI STUDIO \342\200\224 COMPLETE ANDROID APP DEVELOPMENT PROMPT\n\nAPP NAME: COLORS OF FAITH \342\200\224 BIBLE FOR KIDS\n\nAct as a senior Android developer, Christian educational content designer, and professional mobile UI/UX designer. Build a complete, working, polished Android application named Colors of Faith \342\200\224 Bible for Kids.\n\nThe application teaches children the Christian message of salvation through the traditional Colors of Salvation / Wordless Book concept. Children will explore different colors, learn what each color represents, read related Bible verses, answer quizzes, and grow in their understanding of God\'s Word.\n\nThe app must have a beautiful, colorful Christian identity that is Bible-centered and appropriate for children. Do not use Catholic-specific devotional imagery, symbols, or artwork.\n\nDo not simply provide a plan, tutorial, wireframe, or mockup. Generate the actual application code and implement the functional screens.\n\n1. ANDROID DEVELOPMENT REQUIREMENTS\n\nBuild a native Android application using:\n\nKotlin.\n\nJetpack Compose.\n\nMaterial 3.\n\nAndroid Studio-compatible Gradle configuration.\n\nModern, reusable UI components.\n\nA simple, maintainable architecture.\n\nLocal device storage for progress, bookmarks, and quiz scores.\n\nTechnical requirements:\n\nApplication name: Colors of Faith.\n\nSuggested application ID: com.colorsfaith.biblekids.\n\nUse the latest stable, mutually compatible Android dependencies available in the environment.\n\nUse a suitable minimum Android SDK and a current compile SDK supported by the installed toolchain.\n\nSupport portrait orientation and responsive layouts for different phone sizes.\n\nInclude Android back navigation.\n\nUse accessible touch targets and readable text.\n\nOptimize for low-end Android phones.\n\nKeep the application lightweight.\n\nAvoid unnecessary dependencies.\n\nDo not require Firebase, a backend server, an account, or internet connectivity.\n\nDo not request unnecessary Android permissions.\n\nAll essential lessons, Bible verses, quizzes, illustrations, and progress tracking must work offline.\n\nUse local JSON, Kotlin data classes, or another appropriate offline content structure for lesson data.\n\nUse DataStore or Room where appropriate. For this small application, choose the simplest reliable storage solution.\n\nGenerate complete source code, resources, Gradle configuration, and AndroidManifest.xml.\n\n2. CHRISTIAN VISUAL IDENTITY \342\200\224 VERY IMPORTANT\n\nThe entire application must have a general, Bible-centered Christian identity.\n\nDo not create a Catholic-inspired application.\n\nDo not include Catholic-specific devotional objects, symbols, or imagery, including:\n\nRosaries or prayer beads.\n\nStatues or devotional portraits of Mary or saints.\n\nMarian devotional imagery.\n\nCatholic saint cards or traditional Catholic devotional illustrations.\n\nPapal symbols or Vatican imagery.\n\nCatholic altars, elaborate Catholic vestments, or Catholic-specific ceremonial objects.\n\nCatholic sacred-heart devotional artwork.\n\nUse general Christian imagery centered on the Holy Bible, Jesus Christ, the cross, God\'s love, salvation, prayer, creation, and Scripture.\n\nPreferred visual elements include:\n\nAn open Holy Bible.\n\nA simple Christian cross.\n\nGolden rays of light.\n\nColorful rainbows and flowing ribbons.\n\nDoves symbolizing peace.\n\nStars, clouds, and beautiful skies.\n\nGreen plants and seedlings representing spiritual growth.\n\nHearts representing love.\n\nFriendly cartoon children reading the Bible.\n\nChildren helping others and learning biblical values.\n\nGentle Bible-story illustrations appropriate for young children.\n\nA simple cross and open Bible are preferred symbols. Do not add denominational symbols.\n\nCreate original illustrations or use locally bundled vector artwork. Do not rely on remote images that may fail when the device is offline.\n\nDo not use emojis as substitutes for the main illustrations or app icons.\n\n3. COLORFUL CHRISTIAN SPLASH SCREEN\n\nCreate a stunning, vibrant, polished splash screen that immediately communicates Christian faith, joy, hope, and Bible learning.\n\nVisual composition\n\nA beautiful gradient background blending sky blue, purple, golden yellow, and warm orange.\n\nA large, glowing open Holy Bible at the center.\n\nA simple Christian cross rising behind or above the Bible.\n\nSoft golden rays of light surrounding the cross and Bible.\n\nSix flowing ribbons or colorful arcs representing gold, black, red, white, green, and blue.\n\nSmall stars, clouds, and subtle sparkles.\n\nOptional friendly cartoon children holding Bibles near the bottom.\n\nSmooth, gentle animation for the light rays or floating stars, provided it does not delay startup.\n\nText\n\nApp title:\n\n\"Colors of Faith\"\n\nSubtitle:\n\n\"Discover God\'s Love Through His Word\"\n\nDesign requirements\n\nMake the title prominent and easy to read.\n\nUse beautiful, rounded typography suitable for children.\n\nUse balanced spacing and professional composition.\n\nMake the splash screen colorful rather than plain white or minimalist.\n\nUse a custom illustration instead of relying on generic stock imagery.\n\nEnsure the splash screen looks attractive on different screen sizes.\n\nBundle all assets locally.\n\nKeep the splash screen brief and launch the home screen smoothly.\n\nRespect Android\'s native splash-screen requirements while transitioning to the custom illustrated welcome screen.\n\nThe splash screen must look like a professionally designed Christian children\'s Bible application.\n\n4. HOME SCREEN\n\nCreate a welcoming home screen with a warm cream background, colorful cards, rounded corners, and friendly illustrations.\n\nAt the top, display:\n\nA small app logo featuring an open Bible and simple cross.\n\n\"Hello, Little Bible Explorer!\"\n\nA short message: \"Let\'s discover God\'s Word together!\"\n\nInclude these main navigation cards:\n\nLearn the Colors\n\nSix colorful cards representing the lessons.\n\nSubtitle: \"Discover what each color teaches us.\"\n\nBible Verses\n\nAn illustrated open Bible.\n\nSubtitle: \"Read and remember God\'s Word.\"\n\nColor Quiz\n\nA colorful question-mark and star illustration.\n\nSubtitle: \"Test what you\'ve learned.\"\n\nMy Learning Journey\n\nA growing plant with stars.\n\nSubtitle: \"See how far you\'ve learned.\"\n\nPrayer Time\n\nA gentle Christian illustration.\n\nSubtitle: \"Talk to God through prayer.\"\n\nParents & Teachers\n\nAn open Bible illustration.\n\nSubtitle: \"Helpful guides for teaching children.\"\n\nUse a responsive two-column grid where screen width permits, with a single-column layout on smaller devices.\n\nEvery card must be clickable and navigate to a fully implemented screen.\n\nAdd a small, unobtrusive footer:\n\n\"Learn His Word. Grow in His Love.\"\n\n5. THE SIX COLORS OF SALVATION\n\nCreate six complete lessons. Each lesson must contain:\n\nA distinct color theme.\n\nA custom illustration.\n\nLesson title.\n\nSimple child-friendly explanation.\n\nAccurate KJV Bible verses.\n\nA practical application.\n\nA short prayer.\n\nA \"Remember This\" takeaway.\n\nA button to start the quiz.\n\nA bookmark button.\n\nPrevious and next lesson navigation.\n\nUse simple language suitable for children ages 4\342\200\22312. Avoid frightening, graphic, or shame-inducing explanations.\n\nLESSON 1 \342\200\224 GOLD: GOD\'S GLORY AND HEAVEN\n\nColor: Gold or warm yellow.\n\nIllustration: A beautiful golden sky, radiant light, and a peaceful kingdom-inspired landscape.\n\nMeaning:\n\nGold reminds us of God\'s glory, His perfect kingdom, and the wonderful hope of eternal life through Jesus Christ.\n\nChild-friendly explanation:\n\n\"God is holy, loving, and wonderful. The Bible tells us about His kingdom and His promise of eternal life. Through Jesus, we can know God and receive His gift of life.\"\n\nBible verses, King James Version:\n\nRevelation 21:21\n\n\"And the twelve gates were twelve pearls; every several gate was of one pearl: and the street of the city was pure gold, as it were transparent glass.\"\n\nJohn 14:2\n\n\"In my Father\'s house are many mansions: if it were not so, I would have told you. I go to prepare a place for you.\"\n\nRomans 6:23\n\n\"For the wages of sin is death; but the gift of God is eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord.\"\n\nPractical application:\n\n\"Remember that God loves you and offers eternal life through Jesus. You can thank Him for His promises.\"\n\nPrayer:\n\n\"Dear God, thank You for Your wonderful promises and for loving me. Help me learn more about You and follow Jesus every day. Amen.\"\n\nRemember This:\n\n\"God gives eternal life through Jesus Christ.\"\n\nImportant: Do not teach that money, good behavior, or completing the app\'s lessons earns a place in heaven.\n\nLESSON 2 \342\200\224 BLACK: OUR NEED FOR FORGIVENESS\n\nColor: Black or deep charcoal.\n\nIllustration: A dark background gradually transitioning into warm light, representing our need for God\'s forgiveness.\n\nMeaning:\n\nBlack represents sin and our need for forgiveness and reconciliation with God.\n\nChild-friendly explanation:\n\n\"Sin means disobeying God and choosing what is wrong. Everyone has sinned. But God loves us, and He offers forgiveness through Jesus Christ.\"\n\nBible verses, King James Version:\n\nRomans 3:23\n\n\"For all have sinned, and come short of the glory of God;\"\n\nRomans 6:23\n\n\"For the wages of sin is death; but the gift of God is eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord.\"\n\n1 John 1:9\n\n\"If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.\"\n\nPractical application:\n\n\"When you do something wrong, tell the truth, ask God for forgiveness, and try to make things right with anyone you have hurt.\"\n\nPrayer:\n\n\"Dear God, I know that I sometimes make wrong choices. Please forgive me and help me choose what is right. Thank You for loving me. Amen.\"\n\nRemember This:\n\n\"God loves us and offers forgiveness.\"\n\nImportant: Never use frightening images, graphic depictions of punishment, or language that makes children feel worthless or beyond God\'s love.\n\nLESSON 3 \342\200\224 RED: JESUS\' LOVE AND SACRIFICE\n\nColor: Bright red.\n\nIllustration: A simple cross against a beautiful sunset with warm light, representing the love of Jesus Christ.\n\nMeaning:\n\nRed reminds us of Jesus\' sacrifice on the cross and His great love for us.\n\nChild-friendly explanation:\n\n\"Jesus loves us so much that He died on the cross for our sins and rose again. Through Jesus, we can receive God\'s forgiveness and begin a new life with Him.\"\n\nBible verses, King James Version:\n\nJohn 3:16\n\n\"For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life.\"\n\nRomans 5:8\n\n\"But God commendeth his love toward us, in that, while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us.\"\n\n1 Corinthians 15:3\342\200\2234\n\n\"For I delivered unto you first of all that which I also received, how that Christ died for our sins according to the scriptures; And that he was buried, and that he rose again the third day according to the scriptures:\"\n\nPractical application:\n\n\"Remember Jesus\' love for you. Trust Him, thank Him, and show love to others.\"\n\nPrayer:\n\n\"Lord Jesus, thank You for loving me, dying for my sins, and rising again. Help me trust You and follow Your Word. Amen.\"\n\nRemember This:\n\n\"Jesus loves us and gave His life for us.\"\n\nImportant: Keep the cross illustration symbolic and child-friendly. Do not show blood, wounds, graphic crucifixion scenes, or frightening imagery.\n\nLESSON 4 \342\200\224 WHITE: FORGIVENESS AND A CLEAN HEART\n\nColor: White.\n\nIllustration: A white dove, white flowers, and gentle sunlight.\n\nMeaning:\n\nWhite represents forgiveness, cleansing from sin, and the new life God gives through Jesus.\n\nChild-friendly explanation:\n\n\"When we turn to God and trust in Jesus, God forgives us and makes us new. He helps us grow in love, honesty, kindness, and obedience.\"\n\nBible verses, King James Version:\n\nIsaiah 1:18\n\n\"Come now, and let us reason together, saith the LORD: though your sins be as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow; though they be red like crimson, they shall be as wool.\"\n\nPsalm 51:10\n\n\"Create in me a clean heart, O God; and renew a right spirit within me.\"\n\n1 John 1:9\n\n\"If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.\"\n\nPractical application:\n\n\"Tell the truth, forgive others, and ask for forgiveness when you make mistakes.\"\n\nPrayer:\n\n\"Dear God, thank You for forgiving me. Give me a clean heart and help me become more loving, honest, and kind. Amen.\"\n\nRemember This:\n\n\"God forgives us and helps us grow.\"\n\nLESSON 5 \342\200\224 GREEN: GROWING IN FAITH\n\nColor: Green.\n\nIllustration: A bright green seedling growing in rich soil, surrounded by sunlight and tiny leaves.\n\nMeaning:\n\nGreen represents new life and spiritual growth.\n\nChild-friendly explanation:\n\n\"Just as a plant needs water and sunlight, our faith grows when we learn God\'s Word, pray, trust Him, and show love to others.\"\n\nBible verses, King James Version:\n\n2 Peter 3:18\n\n\"But grow in grace, and in the knowledge of our Lord and Saviour Jesus Christ. To him be glory both now and for ever. Amen.\"\n\nPsalm 1:2\342\200\2233\n\n\"But his delight is in the law of the LORD; and in his law doth he meditate day and night.\"\n\n\"And he shall be like a tree planted by the rivers of water, that bringeth forth his fruit in his season; his leaf also shall not wither; and whatsoever he doeth shall prosper.\"\n\nGalatians 5:22\342\200\22323\n\n\"But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, longsuffering, gentleness, goodness, faith,\"\n\n\"Meekness, temperance: against such there is no law.\"\n\nPractical application:\n\n\"Learn one Bible verse, pray, help someone, or practice kindness every day.\"\n\nPrayer:\n\n\"Dear God, help my faith grow stronger every day. Teach me to love others, follow Your Word, and show the fruit of Your Spirit. Amen.\"\n\nRemember This:\n\n\"We can grow in faith every day.\"\n\nLESSON 6 \342\200\224 BLUE: TRUSTING GOD AND FOLLOWING JESUS\n\nColor: Blue.\n\nIllustration: A peaceful blue sky, gentle flowing water, and rays of sunlight.\n\nMeaning:\n\nBlue is an additional teaching color used in this app to represent faith, trust, hope, and following Jesus. Explain that this is a teaching association, not a universal biblical definition of blue.\n\nChild-friendly explanation:\n\n\"We cannot always know what will happen next, but we can trust God and follow Jesus. We can pray, read the Bible, and ask God to help us make wise choices.\"\n\nBible verses, King James Version:\n\nProverbs 3:5\342\200\2236\n\n\"Trust in the LORD with all thine heart; and lean not unto thine own understanding.\"\n\n\"In all thy ways acknowledge him, and he shall direct thy paths.\"\n\nHebrews 11:1\n\n\"Now faith is the substance of things hoped for, the evidence of things not seen.\"\n\nJohn 14:6\n\n\"Jesus saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me.\"\n\nPractical application:\n\n\"When you feel worried or need help making a choice, pray, remember God\'s Word, and talk to a trusted parent or responsible adult.\"\n\nPrayer:\n\n\"Dear God, help me trust You even when I do not understand everything. Guide my choices and help me follow Jesus. Amen.\"\n\nRemember This:\n\n\"We can trust God and follow Jesus.\"\n\n6. BIBLE VERSE LIBRARY\n\nCreate a separate Bible Verses screen.\n\nRequirements:\n\nDisplay verses organized by color and lesson.\n\nShow the verse reference prominently.\n\nDisplay the complete verse text in KJV.\n\nAllow users to browse all verses associated with each lesson.\n\nProvide a search field for Bible verse references, words, and phrases.\n\nAllow users to bookmark favorite verses.\n\nAllow users to copy verse text and references.\n\nAdd a \"Read Aloud\" button using Android\'s built-in TextToSpeech functionality.\n\nWork fully offline.\n\nProvide a clear message when no search results are found.\n\nDo not claim to contain the complete Bible. This is a collection of verses selected for the app\'s lessons.\n\nAll quoted KJV verses must be checked for accuracy. Do not invent, paraphrase, or misattribute text presented as an exact Bible quotation. Store Bible references and verse text separately so they can be verified.\n\n7. COLOR LESSON SCREEN\n\nWhen a child taps a color, display a dedicated lesson page.\n\nInclude:\n\nA large, beautiful color-themed illustration.\n\nThe color name and lesson title.\n\nA \"What Does This Color Mean?\" section.\n\nA short explanation using child-friendly language.\n\nA \"Bible Verse\" card with the KJV text and reference.\n\nA \"What Can I Learn?\" practical application.\n\nA \"Let\'s Pray\" card with the lesson prayer.\n\nA \"Remember This\" takeaway.\n\nA bookmark button.\n\nA \"Take the Quiz\" button.\n\nPrevious and Next navigation.\n\nA button to return to all six lessons.\n\nUse locally bundled illustrations and reusable Compose components.\n\nDo not overcrowd the screen. Use clear sections, comfortable spacing, readable text, and a scrollable layout.\n\n8. MULTIPLE-CHOICE QUIZ\n\nImplement a complete quiz system for all six colors.\n\nRequirements:\n\nAt least five questions per lesson.\n\nFour answer choices per question.\n\nExactly one correct answer.\n\nImmediate feedback after each selection.\n\nA short explanation of the correct answer.\n\nA Next Question button.\n\nA final score screen.\n\nA Try Again button.\n\nLocal score storage.\n\nBest score per lesson.\n\nStars or badges for encouragement.\n\nA way to return to the lesson.\n\nUse encouraging messages such as:\n\n\"Great job!\"\n\n\"Keep learning!\"\n\n\"Wonderful effort!\"\n\n\"You\'re growing in God\'s Word!\"\n\n\"Let\'s try that one again!\"\n\nDo not shame children or use negative messages for incorrect answers.\n\nExample:\n\nQuestion: What does the red color remind us of?\n\nA. Jesus\' love and sacrifice.\n\nB. The importance of money.\n\nC. Winning every game.\n\nD. Being better than others.\n\nCorrect answer: A.\n\nExplanation: Red reminds us of Jesus\' love and His sacrifice for us.\n\nCreate accurate, age-appropriate questions based on each lesson and its Bible verses. Do not use trick questions or denominational disputes.\n\nQuiz results must never determine whether a child can access a Bible lesson.\n\n9. MY LEARNING JOURNEY\n\nCreate a progress screen that includes:\n\nSix color lessons.\n\nCompleted lessons.\n\nLessons not yet completed.\n\nBible verses learned.\n\nQuiz scores.\n\nBest score for each lesson.\n\nTotal stars earned.\n\nA colorful progress bar.\n\nA completion badge when all six lessons have been explored.\n\nUse local storage so progress remains available after closing and reopening the app.\n\nDo not include public rankings, competitive leaderboards, or social sharing.\n\nMake the screen encouraging, friendly, and visually attractive.\n\n10. PRAYER TIME\n\nCreate a simple Prayer Time screen containing short, child-friendly Christian prayers.\n\nInclude:\n\nMorning Prayer.\n\nEvening Prayer.\n\nPrayer for Wisdom.\n\nPrayer for Forgiveness.\n\nPrayer for Family.\n\nPrayer for Friends.\n\nPrayer for Courage.\n\nThank You, God Prayer.\n\nEach prayer must include a title, a short prayer, and a relevant Bible reference where appropriate.\n\nClearly distinguish original prayers written for the app from direct Bible quotations.\n\nUse gentle backgrounds, simple illustrations, and readable text.\n\nInclude a button to read each prayer aloud using offline text-to-speech when available.\n\nDo not present these prayers as mandatory formulas or suggest that a child must repeat them perfectly.11. PARENTS AND TEACHERS GUIDE\n\nCreate a dedicated guide with:\n\nA brief introduction to the Colors of Salvation.\n\nThe meaning of each color.\n\nSuggested discussion questions.\n\nIdeas for family devotion time.\n\nSunday school lesson suggestions.\n\nTips for explaining sin, forgiveness, Jesus\' sacrifice, and salvation without frightening or shaming children.\n\nEncouragement to answer difficult questions gently and honestly.\n\nA reminder that the colors are teaching aids, not objects with spiritual power.\n\nExample questions:\n\nWhat does this color teach us about God?\n\nWhat Bible verse did you learn today?\n\nWhat did Jesus do for us?\n\nHow can you show love to someone this week?\n\nWhat would you like to ask God about today?\n\nKeep this section practical and concise.\n\n12. BOOKMARKS AND FAVORITES\n\nAllow children to bookmark:\n\nFavorite color lessons.\n\nFavorite Bible verses.\n\nFavorite prayers.\n\nCreate a Favorites screen where bookmarked content can be viewed and opened.\n\nStore bookmarks locally on the device.\n\nAllow users to remove bookmarks easily.\n\n13. APP ICON AND LAUNCHER DESIGN\n\nCreate a custom Android launcher icon.\n\nDesign:\n\nA colorful open Bible.\n\nA simple cross rising from the center of the Bible.\n\nSix flowing color bands or a subtle rainbow.\n\nA clean, bold composition that remains recognizable at small sizes.\n\nA friendly, polished, child-appropriate illustration style.\n\nDo not include small text in the icon.\n\nDo not use Catholic devotional symbols, saint imagery, rosaries, Marian imagery, or Catholic-specific iconography.\n\nGenerate the required Android adaptive icon assets, including foreground and background layers.\n\nUse the same visual identity across the splash screen, home screen, lesson illustrations, and launcher icon.\n\n14. COLOR PALETTE AND UI DESIGN\n\nUse this initial palette:\n\nGold: #F6C945\n\nDark charcoal: #30313A\n\nRed: #E84C4F\n\nWhite: #FFFFFF\n\nGreen: #43A66C\n\nBlue: #4C91E2\n\nBackground cream: #FFF9F0\n\nMain text: #263238\n\nAccent purple: #8B72D9\n\nAccent orange: #FF9F43\n\nSoft sky blue: #DFF3FF\n\nDesign style:\n\nRounded cards with 18\342\200\22324 dp corner radii.\n\nLarge, friendly typography.\n\nColorful gradients where appropriate.\n\nSoft shadows.\n\nSimple transitions and subtle animations.\n\nGenerous spacing.\n\nClear visual hierarchy.\n\nStrong contrast and accessibility.\n\nTouch-friendly controls.\n\nConsistent icons and illustrations.\n\nUse Material 3 while customizing it to achieve a distinctive Christian children\'s educational appearance.\n\nAvoid a generic business-dashboard look, excessive white space, monochrome religious artwork, or an overly plain interface.\n\nUse a consistent illustration style across the entire application.\n\n15. ACCESSIBILITY AND CHILD-FRIENDLY EXPERIENCE\n\nUse readable font sizes.\n\nProvide adequate contrast.\n\nGive buttons clear labels.\n\nAdd content descriptions to meaningful illustrations.\n\nAvoid flashing animations and excessive motion.\n\nKeep interactions simple.\n\nDo not rely on color alone to explain the meaning of a lesson; always display the color name and explanation.\n\nSupport scrolling on smaller screens.\n\nPrevent text from being clipped.\n\nProvide sensible empty states.\n\nEnsure all interactive controls perform their intended actions.\n\nMake the app enjoyable for children ages 4\342\200\22312, with a design that parents and teachers will also appreciate.\n\n16. PRIVACY AND OFFLINE FUNCTIONALITY\n\nThis application does not need registration or online accounts.\n\nRequirements:\n\nNo Firebase.\n\nNo backend server.\n\nNo advertising.\n\nNo third-party analytics.\n\nNo account creation.\n\nNo collection of personal information.\n\nNo camera, contacts, location, or microphone permissions.\n\nNo chat or public social features.\n\nNo remote images required for core functionality.\n\nNo mandatory internet connection.\n\nStore progress, bookmarks, and quiz scores locally.\n\nThe app must open and remain fully usable in airplane mode.\n\nInclude a short About and Privacy screen explaining that the app works offline and stores learning progress locally on the device.\n\nIf the app uses Android TextToSpeech, make the read-aloud feature optional and provide a graceful fallback if no suitable speech engine or voice is available.\n\n17. NAVIGATION STRUCTURE\n\nImplement functional navigation for:\n\nSplash Screen.\n\nHome.\n\nLearn the Colors.\n\nIndividual Color Lesson.\n\nBible Verses.\n\nVerse Search Results.\n\nFavorites.\n\nColor Quiz.\n\nQuiz Results.\n\nMy Learning Journey.\n\nPrayer Time.\n\nParents & Teachers.\n\nAbout and Privacy.\n\nUse a simple bottom navigation bar for the primary destinations, such as Home, Learn, Bible, and Progress. Place secondary destinations in the home screen or a clearly labeled menu.\n\nKeep navigation intuitive and appropriate for children.\n\nImplement Android back navigation correctly. Preserve lesson and quiz state where appropriate.\n\nDo not leave any screen as a placeholder.\n\n18. CODE QUALITY AND PROJECT STRUCTURE\n\nOrganize the application into logical packages, for example:\n\ndata \342\200\224 lessons, verses, prayers, and quiz questions.\n\nmodel \342\200\224 Kotlin data classes.\n\nui \342\200\224 reusable components and theme.\n\nui.screens \342\200\224 individual screens.\n\nnavigation \342\200\224 routes and navigation graph.\n\nstorage \342\200\224 bookmarks and progress persistence.\n\nutil \342\200\224 helper functions.\n\nUse reusable composables for:\n\nColor lesson cards.\n\nBible verse cards.\n\nQuiz answer buttons.\n\nProgress indicators.\n\nPrayer cards.\n\nNavigation controls.\n\nKeep content data separate from UI implementation.\n\nUse stable keys for list items and avoid unnecessary recompositions.\n\nDo not put the entire application into one massive Kotlin file.\n\nEnsure the project contains every required file and resource.\n\n19. REQUIRED TESTING AND VALIDATION\n\nBefore completing the project, verify:\n\nThe app builds successfully.\n\nThe splash screen opens correctly.\n\nThe home screen displays all sections.\n\nAll six color lessons open correctly.\n\nBible verse text and references are accurate.\n\nVerse search works offline.\n\nBookmarks can be added and removed.\n\nQuizzes have four answer options and one correct answer per question.\n\nQuiz scoring is correct.\n\nQuiz progress persists locally.\n\nLesson completion persists after restarting the app.\n\nText-to-speech works when available and fails gracefully otherwise.\n\nNavigation and Android back behavior work correctly.\n\nNo required screen is incomplete.\n\nNo remote connection is needed to access core content.\n\nThe app runs in airplane mode.\n\nThe interface fits small Android screens.\n\nThe launcher icon and splash screen use the same Christian visual identity.\n\nNo Catholic-specific imagery or devotional symbols are present.\n\nNo missing imports, unresolved dependencies, or obvious compilation errors remain.\n\nIf a dependency or API is incompatible with the installed Android toolchain, replace it with a compatible alternative rather than leaving the project broken.\n\nDo not claim successful testing unless the build and relevant functionality have actually been verified.\n\n20. FINAL DELIVERABLE\n\nGenerate a complete Android Studio project containing:\n\nKotlin source files.\n\nJetpack Compose screens.\n\nNavigation implementation.\n\nAll six color lessons.\n\nKJV Bible verse content.\n\nAt least 30 multiple-choice quiz questions.\n\nPrayer content.\n\nLocal progress storage.\n\nBookmark functionality.\n\nSearch functionality.\n\nSplash screen.\n\nCustom launcher icon.\n\nLocally bundled illustrations.\n\nMaterial 3 theme and colors.\n\nAndroidManifest.xml.\n\nGradle configuration.\n\nRequired resources.\n\nAny required preview functions for Android Studio.\n\nClear instructions for opening, building, running, and testing the application.\n\nMake the app functional before focusing on optional polish.\n\nIf the environment cannot generate all files in a single response, implement the project in manageable parts and clearly identify which files are complete and which remain. Do not silently omit essential features.\n\nFINAL DESIGN OBJECTIVE\n\nCreate a beautiful, vibrant, lightweight, fully offline Christian children\'s Bible application.\n\nThe first impression must be a colorful Christian splash screen with an open Holy Bible, a simple cross, radiant light, and joyful colors.\n\nThe entire app must feature original, child-friendly Christian illustrations rather than Catholic-specific devotional artwork.\n\nThe educational experience must focus on the message of salvation, the love of Jesus Christ, forgiveness, faith, and spiritual growth through Bible verses and interactive lessons.\n\nBuild the actual working Android application, not just a concept or design proposal.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nInstructions: If you need more context from the user you must first ask the user some questions using the ask_question tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    items {
      item {
        text_block {
          content: "---\ntype: \"feature\"\ntitle: \"Build an Android app\"\nicon: \"android_color\"\n---\n\n"
        }
      }
    }
    items {
      item {
        text_block {
          content: "---\ntype: \"feature\"\ntitle: \"Enable high thinking\"\nicon: \"network_intelligence\"\n---\n\nYou MUST add thinking mode to the app where relevant to handle users\' most complex queries. You MUST use the gemini-3.1-pro-preview model and set `thinkingLevel` to `ThinkingLevel.HIGH`. Do not set `maxOutputTokens`."
        }
      }
    }
    items {
      text: "GOOGLE AI STUDIO \342\200\224 COMPLETE ANDROID APP DEVELOPMENT PROMPT\n\nAPP NAME: COLORS OF FAITH \342\200\224 BIBLE FOR KIDS\n\nAct as a senior Android developer, Christian educational content designer, and professional mobile UI/UX designer. Build a complete, working, polished Android application named Colors of Faith \342\200\224 Bible for Kids.\n\nThe application teaches children the Christian message of salvation through the traditional Colors of Salvation / Wordless Book concept. Children will explore different colors, learn what each color represents, read related Bible verses, answer quizzes, and grow in their understanding of God\'s Word.\n\nThe app must have a beautiful, colorful Christian identity that is Bible-centered and appropriate for children. Do not use Catholic-specific devotional imagery, symbols, or artwork.\n\nDo not simply provide a plan, tutorial, wireframe, or mockup. Generate the actual application code and implement the functional screens.\n\n1. ANDROID DEVELOPMENT REQUIREMENTS\n\nBuild a native Android application using:\n\nKotlin.\n\nJetpack Compose.\n\nMaterial 3.\n\nAndroid Studio-compatible Gradle configuration.\n\nModern, reusable UI components.\n\nA simple, maintainable architecture.\n\nLocal device storage for progress, bookmarks, and quiz scores.\n\nTechnical requirements:\n\nApplication name: Colors of Faith.\n\nSuggested application ID: com.colorsfaith.biblekids.\n\nUse the latest stable, mutually compatible Android dependencies available in the environment.\n\nUse a suitable minimum Android SDK and a current compile SDK supported by the installed toolchain.\n\nSupport portrait orientation and responsive layouts for different phone sizes.\n\nInclude Android back navigation.\n\nUse accessible touch targets and readable text.\n\nOptimize for low-end Android phones.\n\nKeep the application lightweight.\n\nAvoid unnecessary dependencies.\n\nDo not require Firebase, a backend server, an account, or internet connectivity.\n\nDo not request unnecessary Android permissions.\n\nAll essential lessons, Bible verses, quizzes, illustrations, and progress tracking must work offline.\n\nUse local JSON, Kotlin data classes, or another appropriate offline content structure for lesson data.\n\nUse DataStore or Room where appropriate. For this small application, choose the simplest reliable storage solution.\n\nGenerate complete source code, resources, Gradle configuration, and AndroidManifest.xml.\n\n2. CHRISTIAN VISUAL IDENTITY \342\200\224 VERY IMPORTANT\n\nThe entire application must have a general, Bible-centered Christian identity.\n\nDo not create a Catholic-inspired application.\n\nDo not include Catholic-specific devotional objects, symbols, or imagery, including:\n\nRosaries or prayer beads.\n\nStatues or devotional portraits of Mary or saints.\n\nMarian devotional imagery.\n\nCatholic saint cards or traditional Catholic devotional illustrations.\n\nPapal symbols or Vatican imagery.\n\nCatholic altars, elaborate Catholic vestments, or Catholic-specific ceremonial objects.\n\nCatholic sacred-heart devotional artwork.\n\nUse general Christian imagery centered on the Holy Bible, Jesus Christ, the cross, God\'s love, salvation, prayer, creation, and Scripture.\n\nPreferred visual elements include:\n\nAn open Holy Bible.\n\nA simple Christian cross.\n\nGolden rays of light.\n\nColorful rainbows and flowing ribbons.\n\nDoves symbolizing peace.\n\nStars, clouds, and beautiful skies.\n\nGreen plants and seedlings representing spiritual growth.\n\nHearts representing love.\n\nFriendly cartoon children reading the Bible.\n\nChildren helping others and learning biblical values.\n\nGentle Bible-story illustrations appropriate for young children.\n\nA simple cross and open Bible are preferred symbols. Do not add denominational symbols.\n\nCreate original illustrations or use locally bundled vector artwork. Do not rely on remote images that may fail when the device is offline.\n\nDo not use emojis as substitutes for the main illustrations or app icons.\n\n3. COLORFUL CHRISTIAN SPLASH SCREEN\n\nCreate a stunning, vibrant, polished splash screen that immediately communicates Christian faith, joy, hope, and Bible learning.\n\nVisual composition\n\nA beautiful gradient background blending sky blue, purple, golden yellow, and warm orange.\n\nA large, glowing open Holy Bible at the center.\n\nA simple Christian cross rising behind or above the Bible.\n\nSoft golden rays of light surrounding the cross and Bible.\n\nSix flowing ribbons or colorful arcs representing gold, black, red, white, green, and blue.\n\nSmall stars, clouds, and subtle sparkles.\n\nOptional friendly cartoon children holding Bibles near the bottom.\n\nSmooth, gentle animation for the light rays or floating stars, provided it does not delay startup.\n\nText\n\nApp title:\n\n\"Colors of Faith\"\n\nSubtitle:\n\n\"Discover God\'s Love Through His Word\"\n\nDesign requirements\n\nMake the title prominent and easy to read.\n\nUse beautiful, rounded typography suitable for children.\n\nUse balanced spacing and professional composition.\n\nMake the splash screen colorful rather than plain white or minimalist.\n\nUse a custom illustration instead of relying on generic stock imagery.\n\nEnsure the splash screen looks attractive on different screen sizes.\n\nBundle all assets locally.\n\nKeep the splash screen brief and launch the home screen smoothly.\n\nRespect Android\'s native splash-screen requirements while transitioning to the custom illustrated welcome screen.\n\nThe splash screen must look like a professionally designed Christian children\'s Bible application.\n\n4. HOME SCREEN\n\nCreate a welcoming home screen with a warm cream background, colorful cards, rounded corners, and friendly illustrations.\n\nAt the top, display:\n\nA small app logo featuring an open Bible and simple cross.\n\n\"Hello, Little Bible Explorer!\"\n\nA short message: \"Let\'s discover God\'s Word together!\"\n\nInclude these main navigation cards:\n\nLearn the Colors\n\nSix colorful cards representing the lessons.\n\nSubtitle: \"Discover what each color teaches us.\"\n\nBible Verses\n\nAn illustrated open Bible.\n\nSubtitle: \"Read and remember God\'s Word.\"\n\nColor Quiz\n\nA colorful question-mark and star illustration.\n\nSubtitle: \"Test what you\'ve learned.\"\n\nMy Learning Journey\n\nA growing plant with stars.\n\nSubtitle: \"See how far you\'ve learned.\"\n\nPrayer Time\n\nA gentle Christian illustration.\n\nSubtitle: \"Talk to God through prayer.\"\n\nParents & Teachers\n\nAn open Bible illustration.\n\nSubtitle: \"Helpful guides for teaching children.\"\n\nUse a responsive two-column grid where screen width permits, with a single-column layout on smaller devices.\n\nEvery card must be clickable and navigate to a fully implemented screen.\n\nAdd a small, unobtrusive footer:\n\n\"Learn His Word. Grow in His Love.\"\n\n5. THE SIX COLORS OF SALVATION\n\nCreate six complete lessons. Each lesson must contain:\n\nA distinct color theme.\n\nA custom illustration.\n\nLesson title.\n\nSimple child-friendly explanation.\n\nAccurate KJV Bible verses.\n\nA practical application.\n\nA short prayer.\n\nA \"Remember This\" takeaway.\n\nA button to start the quiz.\n\nA bookmark button.\n\nPrevious and next lesson navigation.\n\nUse simple language suitable for children ages 4\342\200\22312. Avoid frightening, graphic, or shame-inducing explanations.\n\nLESSON 1 \342\200\224 GOLD: GOD\'S GLORY AND HEAVEN\n\nColor: Gold or warm yellow.\n\nIllustration: A beautiful golden sky, radiant light, and a peaceful kingdom-inspired landscape.\n\nMeaning:\n\nGold reminds us of God\'s glory, His perfect kingdom, and the wonderful hope of eternal life through Jesus Christ.\n\nChild-friendly explanation:\n\n\"God is holy, loving, and wonderful. The Bible tells us about His kingdom and His promise of eternal life. Through Jesus, we can know God and receive His gift of life.\"\n\nBible verses, King James Version:\n\nRevelation 21:21\n\n\"And the twelve gates were twelve pearls; every several gate was of one pearl: and the street of the city was pure gold, as it were transparent glass.\"\n\nJohn 14:2\n\n\"In my Father\'s house are many mansions: if it were not so, I would have told you. I go to prepare a place for you.\"\n\nRomans 6:23\n\n\"For the wages of sin is death; but the gift of God is eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord.\"\n\nPractical application:\n\n\"Remember that God loves you and offers eternal life through Jesus. You can thank Him for His promises.\"\n\nPrayer:\n\n\"Dear God, thank You for Your wonderful promises and for loving me. Help me learn more about You and follow Jesus every day. Amen.\"\n\nRemember This:\n\n\"God gives eternal life through Jesus Christ.\"\n\nImportant: Do not teach that money, good behavior, or completing the app\'s lessons earns a place in heaven.\n\nLESSON 2 \342\200\224 BLACK: OUR NEED FOR FORGIVENESS\n\nColor: Black or deep charcoal.\n\nIllustration: A dark background gradually transitioning into warm light, representing our need for God\'s forgiveness.\n\nMeaning:\n\nBlack represents sin and our need for forgiveness and reconciliation with God.\n\nChild-friendly explanation:\n\n\"Sin means disobeying God and choosing what is wrong. Everyone has sinned. But God loves us, and He offers forgiveness through Jesus Christ.\"\n\nBible verses, King James Version:\n\nRomans 3:23\n\n\"For all have sinned, and come short of the glory of God;\"\n\nRomans 6:23\n\n\"For the wages of sin is death; but the gift of God is eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord.\"\n\n1 John 1:9\n\n\"If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.\"\n\nPractical application:\n\n\"When you do something wrong, tell the truth, ask God for forgiveness, and try to make things right with anyone you have hurt.\"\n\nPrayer:\n\n\"Dear God, I know that I sometimes make wrong choices. Please forgive me and help me choose what is right. Thank You for loving me. Amen.\"\n\nRemember This:\n\n\"God loves us and offers forgiveness.\"\n\nImportant: Never use frightening images, graphic depictions of punishment, or language that makes children feel worthless or beyond God\'s love.\n\nLESSON 3 \342\200\224 RED: JESUS\' LOVE AND SACRIFICE\n\nColor: Bright red.\n\nIllustration: A simple cross against a beautiful sunset with warm light, representing the love of Jesus Christ.\n\nMeaning:\n\nRed reminds us of Jesus\' sacrifice on the cross and His great love for us.\n\nChild-friendly explanation:\n\n\"Jesus loves us so much that He died on the cross for our sins and rose again. Through Jesus, we can receive God\'s forgiveness and begin a new life with Him.\"\n\nBible verses, King James Version:\n\nJohn 3:16\n\n\"For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life.\"\n\nRomans 5:8\n\n\"But God commendeth his love toward us, in that, while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us.\"\n\n1 Corinthians 15:3\342\200\2234\n\n\"For I delivered unto you first of all that which I also received, how that Christ died for our sins according to the scriptures; And that he was buried, and that he rose again the third day according to the scriptures:\"\n\nPractical application:\n\n\"Remember Jesus\' love for you. Trust Him, thank Him, and show love to others.\"\n\nPrayer:\n\n\"Lord Jesus, thank You for loving me, dying for my sins, and rising again. Help me trust You and follow Your Word. Amen.\"\n\nRemember This:\n\n\"Jesus loves us and gave His life for us.\"\n\nImportant: Keep the cross illustration symbolic and child-friendly. Do not show blood, wounds, graphic crucifixion scenes, or frightening imagery.\n\nLESSON 4 \342\200\224 WHITE: FORGIVENESS AND A CLEAN HEART\n\nColor: White.\n\nIllustration: A white dove, white flowers, and gentle sunlight.\n\nMeaning:\n\nWhite represents forgiveness, cleansing from sin, and the new life God gives through Jesus.\n\nChild-friendly explanation:\n\n\"When we turn to God and trust in Jesus, God forgives us and makes us new. He helps us grow in love, honesty, kindness, and obedience.\"\n\nBible verses, King James Version:\n\nIsaiah 1:18\n\n\"Come now, and let us reason together, saith the LORD: though your sins be as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow; though they be red like crimson, they shall be as wool.\"\n\nPsalm 51:10\n\n\"Create in me a clean heart, O God; and renew a right spirit within me.\"\n\n1 John 1:9\n\n\"If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.\"\n\nPractical application:\n\n\"Tell the truth, forgive others, and ask for forgiveness when you make mistakes.\"\n\nPrayer:\n\n\"Dear God, thank You for forgiving me. Give me a clean heart and help me become more loving, honest, and kind. Amen.\"\n\nRemember This:\n\n\"God forgives us and helps us grow.\"\n\nLESSON 5 \342\200\224 GREEN: GROWING IN FAITH\n\nColor: Green.\n\nIllustration: A bright green seedling growing in rich soil, surrounded by sunlight and tiny leaves.\n\nMeaning:\n\nGreen represents new life and spiritual growth.\n\nChild-friendly explanation:\n\n\"Just as a plant needs water and sunlight, our faith grows when we learn God\'s Word, pray, trust Him, and show love to others.\"\n\nBible verses, King James Version:\n\n2 Peter 3:18\n\n\"But grow in grace, and in the knowledge of our Lord and Saviour Jesus Christ. To him be glory both now and for ever. Amen.\"\n\nPsalm 1:2\342\200\2233\n\n\"But his delight is in the law of the LORD; and in his law doth he meditate day and night.\"\n\n\"And he shall be like a tree planted by the rivers of water, that bringeth forth his fruit in his season; his leaf also shall not wither; and whatsoever he doeth shall prosper.\"\n\nGalatians 5:22\342\200\22323\n\n\"But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, longsuffering, gentleness, goodness, faith,\"\n\n\"Meekness, temperance: against such there is no law.\"\n\nPractical application:\n\n\"Learn one Bible verse, pray, help someone, or practice kindness every day.\"\n\nPrayer:\n\n\"Dear God, help my faith grow stronger every day. Teach me to love others, follow Your Word, and show the fruit of Your Spirit. Amen.\"\n\nRemember This:\n\n\"We can grow in faith every day.\"\n\nLESSON 6 \342\200\224 BLUE: TRUSTING GOD AND FOLLOWING JESUS\n\nColor: Blue.\n\nIllustration: A peaceful blue sky, gentle flowing water, and rays of sunlight.\n\nMeaning:\n\nBlue is an additional teaching color used in this app to represent faith, trust, hope, and following Jesus. Explain that this is a teaching association, not a universal biblical definition of blue.\n\nChild-friendly explanation:\n\n\"We cannot always know what will happen next, but we can trust God and follow Jesus. We can pray, read the Bible, and ask God to help us make wise choices.\"\n\nBible verses, King James Version:\n\nProverbs 3:5\342\200\2236\n\n\"Trust in the LORD with all thine heart; and lean not unto thine own understanding.\"\n\n\"In all thy ways acknowledge him, and he shall direct thy paths.\"\n\nHebrews 11:1\n\n\"Now faith is the substance of things hoped for, the evidence of things not seen.\"\n\nJohn 14:6\n\n\"Jesus saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me.\"\n\nPractical application:\n\n\"When you feel worried or need help making a choice, pray, remember God\'s Word, and talk to a trusted parent or responsible adult.\"\n\nPrayer:\n\n\"Dear God, help me trust You even when I do not understand everything. Guide my choices and help me follow Jesus. Amen.\"\n\nRemember This:\n\n\"We can trust God and follow Jesus.\"\n\n6. BIBLE VERSE LIBRARY\n\nCreate a separate Bible Verses screen.\n\nRequirements:\n\nDisplay verses organized by color and lesson.\n\nShow the verse reference prominently.\n\nDisplay the complete verse text in KJV.\n\nAllow users to browse all verses associated with each lesson.\n\nProvide a search field for Bible verse references, words, and phrases.\n\nAllow users to bookmark favorite verses.\n\nAllow users to copy verse text and references.\n\nAdd a \"Read Aloud\" button using Android\'s built-in TextToSpeech functionality.\n\nWork fully offline.\n\nProvide a clear message when no search results are found.\n\nDo not claim to contain the complete Bible. This is a collection of verses selected for the app\'s lessons.\n\nAll quoted KJV verses must be checked for accuracy. Do not invent, paraphrase, or misattribute text presented as an exact Bible quotation. Store Bible references and verse text separately so they can be verified.\n\n7. COLOR LESSON SCREEN\n\nWhen a child taps a color, display a dedicated lesson page.\n\nInclude:\n\nA large, beautiful color-themed illustration.\n\nThe color name and lesson title.\n\nA \"What Does This Color Mean?\" section.\n\nA short explanation using child-friendly language.\n\nA \"Bible Verse\" card with the KJV text and reference.\n\nA \"What Can I Learn?\" practical application.\n\nA \"Let\'s Pray\" card with the lesson prayer.\n\nA \"Remember This\" takeaway.\n\nA bookmark button.\n\nA \"Take the Quiz\" button.\n\nPrevious and Next navigation.\n\nA button to return to all six lessons.\n\nUse locally bundled illustrations and reusable Compose components.\n\nDo not overcrowd the screen. Use clear sections, comfortable spacing, readable text, and a scrollable layout.\n\n8. MULTIPLE-CHOICE QUIZ\n\nImplement a complete quiz system for all six colors.\n\nRequirements:\n\nAt least five questions per lesson.\n\nFour answer choices per question.\n\nExactly one correct answer.\n\nImmediate feedback after each selection.\n\nA short explanation of the correct answer.\n\nA Next Question button.\n\nA final score screen.\n\nA Try Again button.\n\nLocal score storage.\n\nBest score per lesson.\n\nStars or badges for encouragement.\n\nA way to return to the lesson.\n\nUse encouraging messages such as:\n\n\"Great job!\"\n\n\"Keep learning!\"\n\n\"Wonderful effort!\"\n\n\"You\'re growing in God\'s Word!\"\n\n\"Let\'s try that one again!\"\n\nDo not shame children or use negative messages for incorrect answers.\n\nExample:\n\nQuestion: What does the red color remind us of?\n\nA. Jesus\' love and sacrifice.\n\nB. The importance of money.\n\nC. Winning every game.\n\nD. Being better than others.\n\nCorrect answer: A.\n\nExplanation: Red reminds us of Jesus\' love and His sacrifice for us.\n\nCreate accurate, age-appropriate questions based on each lesson and its Bible verses. Do not use trick questions or denominational disputes.\n\nQuiz results must never determine whether a child can access a Bible lesson.\n\n9. MY LEARNING JOURNEY\n\nCreate a progress screen that includes:\n\nSix color lessons.\n\nCompleted lessons.\n\nLessons not yet completed.\n\nBible verses learned.\n\nQuiz scores.\n\nBest score for each lesson.\n\nTotal stars earned.\n\nA colorful progress bar.\n\nA completion badge when all six lessons have been explored.\n\nUse local storage so progress remains available after closing and reopening the app.\n\nDo not include public rankings, competitive leaderboards, or social sharing.\n\nMake the screen encouraging, friendly, and visually attractive.\n\n10. PRAYER TIME\n\nCreate a simple Prayer Time screen containing short, child-friendly Christian prayers.\n\nInclude:\n\nMorning Prayer.\n\nEvening Prayer.\n\nPrayer for Wisdom.\n\nPrayer for Forgiveness.\n\nPrayer for Family.\n\nPrayer for Friends.\n\nPrayer for Courage.\n\nThank You, God Prayer.\n\nEach prayer must include a title, a short prayer, and a relevant Bible reference where appropriate.\n\nClearly distinguish original prayers written for the app from direct Bible quotations.\n\nUse gentle backgrounds, simple illustrations, and readable text.\n\nInclude a button to read each prayer aloud using offline text-to-speech when available.\n\nDo not present these prayers as mandatory formulas or suggest that a child must repeat them perfectly.11. PARENTS AND TEACHERS GUIDE\n\nCreate a dedicated guide with:\n\nA brief introduction to the Colors of Salvation.\n\nThe meaning of each color.\n\nSuggested discussion questions.\n\nIdeas for family devotion time.\n\nSunday school lesson suggestions.\n\nTips for explaining sin, forgiveness, Jesus\' sacrifice, and salvation without frightening or shaming children.\n\nEncouragement to answer difficult questions gently and honestly.\n\nA reminder that the colors are teaching aids, not objects with spiritual power.\n\nExample questions:\n\nWhat does this color teach us about God?\n\nWhat Bible verse did you learn today?\n\nWhat did Jesus do for us?\n\nHow can you show love to someone this week?\n\nWhat would you like to ask God about today?\n\nKeep this section practical and concise.\n\n12. BOOKMARKS AND FAVORITES\n\nAllow children to bookmark:\n\nFavorite color lessons.\n\nFavorite Bible verses.\n\nFavorite prayers.\n\nCreate a Favorites screen where bookmarked content can be viewed and opened.\n\nStore bookmarks locally on the device.\n\nAllow users to remove bookmarks easily.\n\n13. APP ICON AND LAUNCHER DESIGN\n\nCreate a custom Android launcher icon.\n\nDesign:\n\nA colorful open Bible.\n\nA simple cross rising from the center of the Bible.\n\nSix flowing color bands or a subtle rainbow.\n\nA clean, bold composition that remains recognizable at small sizes.\n\nA friendly, polished, child-appropriate illustration style.\n\nDo not include small text in the icon.\n\nDo not use Catholic devotional symbols, saint imagery, rosaries, Marian imagery, or Catholic-specific iconography.\n\nGenerate the required Android adaptive icon assets, including foreground and background layers.\n\nUse the same visual identity across the splash screen, home screen, lesson illustrations, and launcher icon.\n\n14. COLOR PALETTE AND UI DESIGN\n\nUse this initial palette:\n\nGold: #F6C945\n\nDark charcoal: #30313A\n\nRed: #E84C4F\n\nWhite: #FFFFFF\n\nGreen: #43A66C\n\nBlue: #4C91E2\n\nBackground cream: #FFF9F0\n\nMain text: #263238\n\nAccent purple: #8B72D9\n\nAccent orange: #FF9F43\n\nSoft sky blue: #DFF3FF\n\nDesign style:\n\nRounded cards with 18\342\200\22324 dp corner radii.\n\nLarge, friendly typography.\n\nColorful gradients where appropriate.\n\nSoft shadows.\n\nSimple transitions and subtle animations.\n\nGenerous spacing.\n\nClear visual hierarchy.\n\nStrong contrast and accessibility.\n\nTouch-friendly controls.\n\nConsistent icons and illustrations.\n\nUse Material 3 while customizing it to achieve a distinctive Christian children\'s educational appearance.\n\nAvoid a generic business-dashboard look, excessive white space, monochrome religious artwork, or an overly plain interface.\n\nUse a consistent illustration style across the entire application.\n\n15. ACCESSIBILITY AND CHILD-FRIENDLY EXPERIENCE\n\nUse readable font sizes.\n\nProvide adequate contrast.\n\nGive buttons clear labels.\n\nAdd content descriptions to meaningful illustrations.\n\nAvoid flashing animations and excessive motion.\n\nKeep interactions simple.\n\nDo not rely on color alone to explain the meaning of a lesson; always display the color name and explanation.\n\nSupport scrolling on smaller screens.\n\nPrevent text from being clipped.\n\nProvide sensible empty states.\n\nEnsure all interactive controls perform their intended actions.\n\nMake the app enjoyable for children ages 4\342\200\22312, with a design that parents and teachers will also appreciate.\n\n16. PRIVACY AND OFFLINE FUNCTIONALITY\n\nThis application does not need registration or online accounts.\n\nRequirements:\n\nNo Firebase.\n\nNo backend server.\n\nNo advertising.\n\nNo third-party analytics.\n\nNo account creation.\n\nNo collection of personal information.\n\nNo camera, contacts, location, or microphone permissions.\n\nNo chat or public social features.\n\nNo remote images required for core functionality.\n\nNo mandatory internet connection.\n\nStore progress, bookmarks, and quiz scores locally.\n\nThe app must open and remain fully usable in airplane mode.\n\nInclude a short About and Privacy screen explaining that the app works offline and stores learning progress locally on the device.\n\nIf the app uses Android TextToSpeech, make the read-aloud feature optional and provide a graceful fallback if no suitable speech engine or voice is available.\n\n17. NAVIGATION STRUCTURE\n\nImplement functional navigation for:\n\nSplash Screen.\n\nHome.\n\nLearn the Colors.\n\nIndividual Color Lesson.\n\nBible Verses.\n\nVerse Search Results.\n\nFavorites.\n\nColor Quiz.\n\nQuiz Results.\n\nMy Learning Journey.\n\nPrayer Time.\n\nParents & Teachers.\n\nAbout and Privacy.\n\nUse a simple bottom navigation bar for the primary destinations, such as Home, Learn, Bible, and Progress. Place secondary destinations in the home screen or a clearly labeled menu.\n\nKeep navigation intuitive and appropriate for children.\n\nImplement Android back navigation correctly. Preserve lesson and quiz state where appropriate.\n\nDo not leave any screen as a placeholder.\n\n18. CODE QUALITY AND PROJECT STRUCTURE\n\nOrganize the application into logical packages, for example:\n\ndata \342\200\224 lessons, verses, prayers, and quiz questions.\n\nmodel \342\200\224 Kotlin data classes.\n\nui \342\200\224 reusable components and theme.\n\nui.screens \342\200\224 individual screens.\n\nnavigation \342\200\224 routes and navigation graph.\n\nstorage \342\200\224 bookmarks and progress persistence.\n\nutil \342\200\224 helper functions.\n\nUse reusable composables for:\n\nColor lesson cards.\n\nBible verse cards.\n\nQuiz answer buttons.\n\nProgress indicators.\n\nPrayer cards.\n\nNavigation controls.\n\nKeep content data separate from UI implementation.\n\nUse stable keys for list items and avoid unnecessary recompositions.\n\nDo not put the entire application into one massive Kotlin file.\n\nEnsure the project contains every required file and resource.\n\n19. REQUIRED TESTING AND VALIDATION\n\nBefore completing the project, verify:\n\nThe app builds successfully.\n\nThe splash screen opens correctly.\n\nThe home screen displays all sections.\n\nAll six color lessons open correctly.\n\nBible verse text and references are accurate.\n\nVerse search works offline.\n\nBookmarks can be added and removed.\n\nQuizzes have four answer options and one correct answer per question.\n\nQuiz scoring is correct.\n\nQuiz progress persists locally.\n\nLesson completion persists after restarting the app.\n\nText-to-speech works when available and fails gracefully otherwise.\n\nNavigation and Android back behavior work correctly.\n\nNo required screen is incomplete.\n\nNo remote connection is needed to access core content.\n\nThe app runs in airplane mode.\n\nThe interface fits small Android screens.\n\nThe launcher icon and splash screen use the same Christian visual identity.\n\nNo Catholic-specific imagery or devotional symbols are present.\n\nNo missing imports, unresolved dependencies, or obvious compilation errors remain.\n\nIf a dependency or API is incompatible with the installed Android toolchain, replace it with a compatible alternative rather than leaving the project broken.\n\nDo not claim successful testing unless the build and relevant functionality have actually been verified.\n\n20. FINAL DELIVERABLE\n\nGenerate a complete Android Studio project containing:\n\nKotlin source files.\n\nJetpack Compose screens.\n\nNavigation implementation.\n\nAll six color lessons.\n\nKJV Bible verse content.\n\nAt least 30 multiple-choice quiz questions.\n\nPrayer content.\n\nLocal progress storage.\n\nBookmark functionality.\n\nSearch functionality.\n\nSplash screen.\n\nCustom launcher icon.\n\nLocally bundled illustrations.\n\nMaterial 3 theme and colors.\n\nAndroidManifest.xml.\n\nGradle configuration.\n\nRequired resources.\n\nAny required preview functions for Android Studio.\n\nClear instructions for opening, building, running, and testing the application.\n\nMake the app functional before focusing on optional polish.\n\nIf the environment cannot generate all files in a single response, implement the project in manageable parts and clearly identify which files are complete and which remain. Do not silently omit essential features.\n\nFINAL DESIGN OBJECTIVE\n\nCreate a beautiful, vibrant, lightweight, fully offline Christian children\'s Bible application.\n\nThe first impression must be a colorful Christian splash screen with an open Holy Bible, a simple cross, radiant light, and joyful colors.\n\nThe entire app must feature original, child-friendly Christian illustrations rather than Catholic-specific devotional artwork.\n\nThe educational experience must focus on the message of salvation, the love of Jesus Christ, forgiveness, faith, and spiritual growth through Bible verses and interactive lessons.\n\nBuild the actual working Android application, not just a concept or design proposal.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nInstructions: If you need more context from the user you must first ask the user some questions using the ask_question tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    }
